{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["The sense of <b>Now the men of Sodom were wicked and sinners</b> is that Scripture holds Lot blameworthy for not holding back from dwelling among them, as in the words of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 13:13). And it speaks further of the merit of the righteous man, in that his lot did not fall in a place where wickedness was, for the lot of the wicked shall not rest upon the portion of the righteous. And all the cities of the plain were wicked and sinners against HaShem exceedingly, for on that account they were overturned — even though all the children of Canaan were men of great abominations, for thus it is written (Leviticus 18:27)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:28:05.224785374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}